No, you would need a separate f() component for each covariate for which you want to have the more complicated model. I would suggest starting with a much simpler model just to get some practice in how to specify inla models in general. There are examples on the r-inla.org <http://r-inla.org> webpages, and for spde models in particular, a link to to the online version of a book on spde models examples.

Finn

