In-Reply-To: <oBShMCTS8WU.EGqIvaQ4AgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <oBShMCTS8WU.EGqIvaQ4AgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/oBShMCTS8WU/m/Imo3t3w-AgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

You mean \lambda in the inla.doc("besagproper2")? This \lambda is a kind of bad parametrization since that \lambda is a mixing in the precision. A better one is the 'bym2' model, see inla.doc("bym2"), where the mixing parameter is in the covariance, thus much easier to interpret [1].

[1] https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/abs/10.1177/0962280216660421?journalCode=smma

best regards,
Elias

